## InventoryService class methods:

### Item Management
- createItem(userId, data) — Insert with UUID, unique SKU validation per user
- updateItem(itemId, userId, updates) — Partial update with ownership validation
- getItem(itemId, userId) — Single item lookup
- listItems(userId, filters?) — List with category/active/search filtering
- deactivateItem(itemId, userId) — Soft-delete (isActive=false)

### Warehouse Management
- createWarehouse(userId, data) — Insert, handles isDefault logic
- listWarehouses(userId) — All active warehouses
- getDefaultWarehouse(userId) — Returns default or creates "Main Warehouse"

### Stock Operations
- adjustStock(userId, itemId, warehouseId, quantity, unitCostCents, movementType, notes?, referenceId?) — Creates movement, upserts stock, recalculates WAC on purchase
- transferStock(userId, itemId, fromWarehouseId, toWarehouseId, quantity, notes?) — Paired transfer_out/transfer_in movements
- getStockLevels(userId, filters?) — JOIN stock+items+warehouses with valuation

### COGS (Weighted Average)
- calculateCOGS(userId, itemId, quantitySold) — Returns { cogsCents, unitCostCents, newAverageCost }
- recalculateWeightedAverage(itemId, existingQty, existingCostCents, newQty, newCostCents) — Pure function

### Reporting
- getMovementHistory(userId, filters?) — Paginated with date/item/type filters
- getValuationReport(userId, asOfDate?) — Full valuation with category breakdown

### Design decisions:
- Lazy table loading (ensureTables) handles concurrent Agent 1 schema work
- Movement type dispatch centralizes add/subtract sign logic
- All amounts in cents (integer), weighted average uses Math.round()
- Singleton export: inventoryService

